cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Warrant, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: "Warrant: an open protocol and reference tool for evidence-gated software built by AI agents"
abstract: >-
  Warrant is an open protocol, with a reference command-line tool, for software that AI
  agents build and maintain while the people accountable for it direct it without
  reading the code. A principal states intent as numbered promises. An examiner runs
  approved checks, some visible to the builder and some hidden, against an exact snapshot
  of the code and records the evidence. A deterministic gatekeeper issues a warrant or a
  denial for each action, such as merge or release. Everything is recorded in an
  append-only, hash-chained ledger.
authors:
